Band Description: Formed in 2004 by Chilean expatriate keyboardist Astrid Silva-Lund and Norwegian percussion saboteur Einar Solheim, Quarteto Calvado became the definitive avatars of the sound. The quartet utilizes a weathered 1973 Fender Rhodes stripped bare to its metal chassis, a muted cornet played with dry West Coast reserve, a battered 7-string Brazilian guitar, and an industrial percussion rig made of discarded zinc sheets, rusted anchor chains, and contact-mic’d ice blocks. Their performances are volatile masterclasses in restrained cool-jazz counterpoint violently interrupted by bursts of tropicalia groove and structural acoustic noise.

